HeroBanner(title="Norns" gradient!="{true}" description="A meta-framework on top of Svelte and SvelteKit. Write components in Pug and Civet with the .n file extension — no template wrappers, no lang attributes, just clean syntax with optional types." align="left")
	+snippet('actions')
		Btn(variant="primary" icon="lucide:rocket" href="/examples") See examples
		Btn(variant="secondary" icon="lucide:github" href="https://github.com/human-synthesis/norns" target="_blank" rel="noopener") GitHub

section.animate-in-delayed.pt-12.space-y-5
	h2.text-2xl.font-semibold.tracking-tight What's in the box
	ul.space-y-4.list-none.p-0
		li.flex.gap-3
			span.feature-bullet ✦
			div(class="text-fg leading-relaxed")
				strong Civet everywhere
				| .  Write
				code count .= $state 0
				| ; reactivity just works. Civet's TypeScript-aware compiler emits ESM-correct output, so runes work without preprocessor magic.
		li.flex.gap-3
			span.feature-bullet ✦
			div(class="text-fg leading-relaxed")
				strong Pug as the default markup
				| .  Concise, indented, no closing tags. Use
				code .n
				|  files for zero boilerplate.
		li.flex.gap-3
			span.feature-bullet ✦
			div(class="text-fg leading-relaxed")
				strong All of SvelteKit
				| .  File-based routing,
				code +page.c
				|  loaders, layouts, adapters — nothing relearned.
		li.flex.gap-3
			span.feature-bullet ✦
			div(class="text-fg leading-relaxed")
				strong Norns runtime
				| .  Feature-folder modularity, DI container, route/page wrappers with valibot validation, and a migrations CLI.
		li.flex.gap-3
			span.feature-bullet ✦
			div(class="text-fg leading-relaxed")
				strong Style how you want
				| .  Norns ships no default styling. This app uses Tailwind v4; pick whatever you like.
